msgid "When dilute hydrochloric acid reacts with sodium carbonate decahydrate,<br>sodium chloride, carbon dioxide and water are formed.<br>A brisk effervescence is seen in the release of carbon dioxide." + "<br>Na<sub>2</sub>CO<sub>3</sub>(s) + 2 HCl → 2NaCl(aq) + CO<sub>2</sub>(g) + H<sub>2</sub>O(l)"
